# Build context exclusions for `podman build` (iso/Containerfile).
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` ships the ENTIRE repo into the build —
# including target/ (~13 GB of host cargo artifacts from local test
# runs) and iso/output/ (built ISOs/images). That made the COPY step
# transfer gigabytes of junk the build never uses: the builder
# compiles into /build/rust via a cache mount, not the host target/.
#
# Keep only source. The COPY drops from ~13 GB to tens of MB.

# Rust build artifacts (host toolchain — irrelevant to the image build)
target/
**/target/

# ISO build outputs + any local images
iso/output/
*.iso

# VCS + editor noise
.git/
.gitignore
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Local cmake build dirs (the Containerfile builds out-of-tree anyway)
build/
**/build/
/tmp/

# Node / misc if ever added
node_modules/

# The container build files themselves don't need to be in the context
# they're invoked from, but harmless to keep — left in so the image can
# self-document if needed.
